id: ops-compatibility-reasons
title: Explain joint compatibility constraints with minimal reason chains
description: "Explain package, host and extension incompatibility from declared version constraints and supported capabilities. Acceptance: three incompatible pins report the exact conflict and compatible ranges; unknown metadata differs from incompatibility; every proposed command is a preview with no installs or configuration edits. Deliver typed SDK and CLI, bounded TOON/JSON, typed refusals and remedies, README and example, no-git and read-only public tracker evidence, model-based replay tests, and CI npm plus Bun release gates."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T10:32:02.370Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-27T15:50:52.895Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[25]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T10:33:17.117Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked: ops status/outdated report individual versions; backend-capabilities.ts verifies list/get/schema support; diagnostic-witnesses.ts reduces declared sufficient facts without solving versions. Sibling starter/presets compatibility-floor tests check manifest admission only. Installed SDK authoring exports checkExtensionManifestCompatibility with the loader-shared inclusive bounds; reuse it for extension checks. This feature explains joint declared dependency ranges and capabilities, leaving actual admission authoritative in core. Explicit bounded metadata input only; no registry fetch, install, configuration edit, tracker mutation, journal, claim or outbox path is introduced. Model tests cover JSON/TOON/file replay and SDK state read-back on a non-git tracker; mutation/recovery/status-role requirements do not apply to this observational path."
  "2026-10-27T10:43:11.513Z",codex-agent,"Focused suite passes 7/7; new module coverage is 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Behavioral revert: remove only intersection satisfiability filtering while retaining Cartesian clauses; the three incompatible pins regression fails 0/1 (expected joint_range_conflict, got installed_pin_conflict). Restoring the implementation returns the test to green. Public main export validation: SDK complete list 160 items, canonical get 1, schema 11 types; 2 components and 2 declarations produce 1 compatible row, 0 incompatible/unknown; JSON 847 bytes, TOON 887 bytes; all read-only source bytes unchanged. Seeded model completed 500 sequences / 3000 operations with SDK read-back of native state and relationships."
  "2026-10-27T10:47:18.493Z",codex-agent,"Linked acceptance passes 7/7 through pm test with 2 workers. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings (321 declarations across 40 files), duplication (0 clones), and production audit (0 vulnerabilities) pass. Clean-home strict health passes; the ambient global pm-github installation uses a newer host and reports version skew under the older pinned CLI, which is not a package tracker defect. Native extension admission remains separate. Output rendering explicitly preserves nested arrays/nulls in TOON and JSON. Additional boundary corpus covers maximum safe version segments, inherited-object refusal, optional-field round trips and 500 exact inclusive/exclusive patch-boundary cases."
  "2026-10-27T10:52:26.916Z",codex-agent,"Final design uses lazy public authoring-export acquisition only for native manifest checks; no argv, executable lookup or symlink-based SDK resolution. A real unsupported Node loader configuration exercises the typed compatibility_sdk_unavailable refusal without SDK mocks. The three-pin packet measures 933 JSON / 1007 TOON bytes. Native metadata is included in packed SDK/CLI acceptance across all six requested launch modes. CI npm/Bun gates and final packed acceptance are pending at push; the feature has no install/configuration mutation path."
  "2026-10-27T11:00:32.422Z",codex-agent,"The final solver reuses parsed semver witnesses and checks feasibility before expanding alternatives; it stops minimum-cardinality search at the first valid witness. Final focused suite again passes 7/7 through pm test, including all 500 operation sequences and 500 exact boundary cases; fresh new-module coverage remains 100% in all four dimensions. Repeating the function-only behavioral revert still fails exactly 0/1. Packed acceptance now uses isolated current Bun 1.4.4, matching the CI setup, because the preinstalled Bun 1.3.5 routes global installs into the local graph. The global fixtures assert that project package metadata stays unchanged. No shared runtime or tool installation is modified."
  "2026-10-27T11:06:37.842Z",codex-agent,"Wide version unions now remain one exact conjunction when expansion would exceed 16 alternatives, preserving npm prerelease rules while keeping agent output bounded. The 256-combination fixture and wildcard case cover this form; final source coverage is 100/100/100/100 after the focused suite plus the supplemental strict-boundary run. Packed topology inspection found that core directory snapshots from an external Bun global graph lose dependency discovery (missing toon dependency). The pinned host explicitly recommends its supported archive installer; global fixtures now use that core capability instead of rebuilding package resolution. This is a host activation UX limitation, not a missing SDK API or a product mutation path."
  "2026-10-27T11:09:37.911Z",codex-agent,"Bun global packed activation now passes: one launch mode, both JSON/TOON checks, and one native SDK consumer, using the core-supported archive install path. Follow-up ops-global-activation-ux retains the directory activation UX limitation. Main advanced only by the 2026.10.27 release commit; the branch includes that release metadata without changing SDK pins. The full six-mode packed rerun and hosted npm/Bun release gates are pending final receipts."
  "2026-10-27T11:19:19.733Z",codex-agent,"Final packed acceptance passes all 6 launch modes, 12 JSON/TOON checks and 4 installed SDK consumers with isolated Bun 1.4.4. The no-git actual CLI now includes native manifest checks under an empty PATH. npm/Bun full release gates remain queued; exact hosted run URLs/counts will be reported in PR checks and the handoff. Greptile reports an expired trial, so no approval is inferred. Current type/test checks, zero-duplication, 322 declarations across 40 source files, zero production vulnerabilities, stable clean-home strict health and changelog checks pass. The new source measures 100% in all four coverage dimensions. Follow-up: ops-global-activation-ux; no pm CLI/SDK API gap remains for this feature."
  "2026-10-27T11:23:30.061Z",codex-agent,"Handoff: implementation and local acceptance are complete. Source/evidence head 171125e has hosted CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/40495421043 still queued; 0 of 4 npm/Bun full release gates have completed and full-suite test counts are unavailable. Earlier CI has remained queued since its initial observation; the queue rules cap waiting at 30 minutes. PR 220 is ready for review, with exact latest run status to be reported in its body and final handoff. Greptile review is unavailable due to the expired trial. Both pm items remain open for orchestrator verification; this claim is being released. No merge or release was performed."
  "2026-10-27T12:09:02.685Z",codex-agent,"Re-review class: never silently discard rejected derived versions and infer an empty version domain. Package-wide search is covering every semver/version decision, SDK/CLI output, packed consumers and no-git paths. Replace handwritten numeric/prerelease successor construction with semver operations and comparator sets; retain library rejections as typed unrepresentable_range evidence naming the affected range. Add max-length prerelease and corpus-based random range-pair regressions, prove failure with only the solver reverted, then run focused and serial full npm/Bun gates with at most two workers. Origin main is already included; no merge is needed."
  "2026-10-27T12:33:43.495Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: compatibility-reasons.ts was the only production module manufacturing semver probe values. It now uses Range comparator sets, intersects, minVersion, inc and validated observed/declared literals only. All library-produced versions are revalidated by semver; rejected values become typed unrepresentable_range records with the range and remedy, including the minimum-conflict path. index.ts and the public SDK share this evaluator. Package-wide search also inspected release-completeness.ts calendar tag formatting and duplication.ts existing-tool major detection: neither synthesizes versions for joint compatibility probes, so changing them would be unrelated. No additional substantive non-blocking findings were present in the supplied finding or GitHub inline reviews. New regressions preserve the existing suite and add maximum-length prereleases, invalid prereleases, numeric overflow, 500 corpus-based random range pairs, JSON/TOON, no-git and packed-consumer coverage. Gate runner concurrency is capped at two with unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-10-27T12:43:52.430Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a non-git scratch copy, restore only the original boundaries and intersection functions (with a signature adapter; all new tests and other production functions unchanged). node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"500 seeded random range pairs\" test/compatibility-ranges.test.ts fails 0/1 on the maximum-length pair: false !== true for compatible range existence. Restoring the new evaluator passes 1/1, completing all 500 sequences. The complete focused compatibility run passes 11/11; worker-cap coverage-gate tests pass 13/13. No tests were removed or weakened; the previous unsupported-range assertion now checks the stronger typed unrepresentable_range classification and its exact range."
  "2026-10-27T12:58:03.684Z",codex-agent,The class check also found a library minVersion shortcut that can miss a strict prerelease successor behind a strict stable lower bound. Added inference packets and randomized compound range pairs with no installed observation; both conjunction and comparator minima now flow through one validated library producer. A function-only revert of feasibleClause fails the same 500-pair property at the new inference case (0/1); restoring it passes 1/1. The initial npm gate was stopped before completion to add this coverage; no pass is claimed for that interrupted run. Full gates are being restarted serially on the corrected source with two workers.
  "2026-10-27T13:39:21.049Z",codex-agent,"The full npm run exposed a stale packed runtime-dependency allowlist: the new required semver dependency was absent from the exact expected list. The assertion now explicitly includes semver; optional-tool absence checks remain intact. Origin main advanced during the run with the Dependabot-owned SDK/changelog pins, so those changes will be merged before final gates. This in-flight run is diagnostic evidence, not a final-head gate pass."
  "2026-10-27T13:52:03.621Z",codex-agent,"Diagnostic full-run receipt before main refresh: 1481 tests, 1474 passed, 4 failed, 1 canceled, 2 optional real-data skips. Three assertion failures are stale exact fixture registries (one runtime dependency list and two renderer command ownership checks); both registries now explicitly include the new dependency/command without weakening their checks. The fourth was the unchanged artifact-reader external timeout under load and will be rerun. The pending release-repair file was canceled when the superseded run was stopped; no completion is inferred. Focused reruns and serial final npm/Bun gates follow the main merge."
  "2026-10-27T14:01:34.625Z",codex-agent,"Main 089e803 is merged, retaining its SDK 2026.10.24 and changelog 2026.10.23 pins. Build and test typecheck pass. Focused main-graph run: 17 tests, 16 pass and one unchanged artifact-reader timeout; all 4 range tests and all 7 renderer tests pass. Import-only diagnosis of the artifact child takes 13.721 seconds versus its 5-second deadline, without reading any artifact; related receipt recorded on ops-gp0d. Per the original saturated-host requirement, final full npm/Bun release gates will run in CI; local targeted and packed checks continue. No test deadline, assertion or threshold was weakened."
  "2026-10-27T14:07:34.969Z",codex-agent,"Corrected source/main-merge head 4d650e1 is pushed. Fresh full npm/Bun CI matrix: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/40517724020 . Previous head CI had only the three exact fixture-list failures in its available Node 26 log (1472 pass, 3 fail, 2 optional skips); its compatibility source coverage was 100 percent in all four dimensions. Both old Windows consumer jobs passed. These are diagnostic receipts only, not final-head approval."
  "2026-10-27T14:18:03.957Z",codex-agent,"Current merged-graph focused coverage passes 11/11 with no failures, cancellations, skips or TODOs: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/compatibility-reasons.test.ts test/compatibility-ranges.test.ts under c8 with 100 percent per-file thresholds. compatibility-reasons.ts measures 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. Includes 500 random range pairs, 500 model sequences/3000 operations, SDK-read native fields/relationships, no-git CLI JSON/TOON, conservative range refusals and native manifest admission checks. Installed CLI routing now passes its focused rerun 1/1; renderer ownership passes 7/7. Expanded packed acceptance is running through the linked pm test."
  "2026-10-27T14:36:24.035Z",codex-agent,"The fresh source/main-merge CI run remains queued through the queue rules' 30-minute observation limit: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/40517724020 . Completed npm/Bun release gates: 0/4; final full-suite test counts are unavailable. No further CI waiting is being used. Local current-graph static checks all pass: typecheck, lint, zero clones across 113 sources and 33064 measured lines, documentation 323 declarations across 40 files; strict clean-home health exits 0 with all 10 checks passing and one advisory retained. Expanded packed acceptance remains independently in progress. The handoff will report CI as pending, never as approval."
  "2026-10-27T14:37:50.844Z",codex-agent,"Final packed acceptance passes through the linked pm test: pm test ops-compatibility-reasons --run --match compatibility-packed.acceptance.ts --progress --timeout 2400. Selected linked command 1/1 passes with zero failure categories: 6 launch modes, 72 JSON/TOON checks, 4 installed SDK consumers and 24 SDK cases, using isolated Bun 1.4.4 and the merged SDK 2026.10.24 pin. All cases run outside Git, including maximum-length tags, named unrepresentable ranges and no-observation inference. Current focused compatibility 11/11 and source coverage 100 percent in all four dimensions; renderer 7/7 and routing 1/1. Both function-only revert proofs are recorded above. The source CI URL remains the pending full npm/Bun evidence (0/4 completed at the 30-minute cap); no full gate pass or external review approval is inferred. PR 220 remains ready for review. Claim is being released; all items remain unclosed."
  "2026-10-27T15:08:58.966Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 class: monotonic evidence under fallible refinement. A proven contradiction must survive subset-reduction refusals; one unknown subset or OR branch must not cancel independently established evidence. Main is already included and the worktree was clean. Plan: tri-state intersection evidence, isolated subset reduction, retain a proven full-set fallback, continue searching other subsets, and explicitly mark unverified minimum cardinality when smaller candidates are unknown. Extend shared adversarial packets across SDK/CLI JSON/TOON, no-git and packed consumers; add 500 seeded exact-domain/metamorphic sequences, preserve all previous tests, and prove a function-only revert fails. Existing public-data receipts remain valid; source and artifact validation will be refreshed without repeating the read-only fleet export."
  "2026-10-27T15:18:54.050Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: compatibility was the only reducer calling a fallible range evaluator under a shared verdict-reset catch. diagnostic-witnesses.ts reduces validated masks without probes; backend-capabilities.ts and diagnostic-plans.ts retain completed rows and isolate read/probe errors per operation/step. SDK, CLI, JSON/TOON and packed paths share explainCompatibility. No additional substantive non-blocking findings appeared in the supplied finding or GitHub review records. Fix uses tri-state branch results, isolated subset refusals, proven full-set fallback, continued subset search for undecided full sets, and optional minimum_unproven when smaller candidates cannot be decided. Behavioral reverts in disposable non-git copies: restoring only minimumConflict's former abort-on-refusal behavior (return-type adapter only) fails the 500-sequence property 0/1; restoring passes 1/1. Restoring only intersection's abort-on-first-branch behavior fails the mixed-alternative regression 0/1; restoring passes 1/1. Source checkout was never reverted, all scratch copies restored and removed, no SDK mocks used. Existing tests remain intact; a new exact finite-pin oracle covers 500 sequences, with old-input replay and declaration permutations."
  "2026-10-27T15:33:29.535Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 focused validation passes 14/14, without failures, cancellations, skips or TODOs; compatibility-reasons.ts retains 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. The new exact-domain property and failure cases pass again through the linked pm test (3/3) after adding witness-id uniqueness/membership and positive-branch certificates. Build, test typecheck, typecheck, lint, duplication (zero clones across 114 sources / 33221 lines) and docstrings (323 declarations across 40 files) pass. Current shared packets now include the reported contradiction, an undecided full set with an independently contradictory subset, and mixed positive/refused OR branches. Expanded packed acceptance is running with the existing deadlines and a credential-free child environment; no previous assertion, deadline or threshold was weakened."
  "2026-10-27T15:45:49.720Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 packed acceptance passes through pm test ops-compatibility-reasons --run --match compatibility-packed.acceptance.ts --progress --timeout 2400: selected command 1/1 passed, six launch modes, 108 JSON/TOON checks and four installed SDK consumers / 36 SDK cases. The reported contradiction, independent subset proof after full-set uncertainty and positive/refused OR branch cases pass in every npm/Bun global/local/x topology outside Git. Repeated both function-only revert proofs on the final strengthened tests: each reverted case 0/1, each restored case 1/1. Strict clean-home health exits zero with all ten checks passing and one advisory retained; production audit finds zero vulnerabilities. The original three-pin example remains 933 JSON / 1007 TOON bytes. The public fleet export receipt (160 items, one canonical get, eleven schema types, 847 JSON / 887 TOON bytes, zero changed source bytes) is retained without repeating that completed validation. Current full-gate evidence will be the fresh CI npm/Bun matrix; no earlier queued run is treated as verification of this fix."
  "2026-10-27T15:50:42.371Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 fix/evidence head 3164256 is pushed. Fresh full npm/Bun release matrix: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/40534763229 (currently queued; 0/4 release gates completed). Main remains included. All local results and both final-test revert proofs are recorded above; there are no remaining substantive supplied review findings. The implementation claim is being released now, leaving the item unclosed. The final metadata-only handoff commit will receive its own exact-head CI verification; its latest run URL and actual counts belong to PR 220 checks/body. No queued, skipped or unavailable check is approval. The queue rule caps observation at 30 minutes, with pending runs handed back rather than keeping an agent waiting indefinitely."
